{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>I saw</b> — It is written in the Torah: <i>הוא ישלח מלאכו לפניך</i> (He will send His angel before you), and <i>וילכו שני המלאכים סדומה</i> (the two angels went to Sodom). And it is written: <i>המלאך הגואל אותי</i> (the angel who redeems me), <i>וישלח מלאך</i> (and He sent an angel), <i>הנה אנכי שולח מלאך</i> (behold, I send an angel), and <i>ומלאך פניו הושיעם</i> (and the angel of His presence saved them). And in the book of Daniel it is explicit: <i>שר יון</i> (the prince of Greece) and <i>שר מלכות פרס</i> (the prince of the kingdom of Persia) and <i>שר השרים</i> (the prince of princes), who is Michael. And the principle: every act of HaShem, may He be exalted, is through the angels, for they are the doers of His word. And the parable that people understand is of a king sitting on his throne who sends his messengers — some on foot and some riding horses — that they may come quickly and inform him of the things in his kingdom. So too here." "<b>and behold a man</b> — an angel, like <i>והאיש גבריאל</i> (and the man Gabriel)." "<b>on a red horse</b> — thus he saw, and there is no need to seek a reason why red. And just so we would not seek a reason why <i>צליל שעורים</i> (silence of barley) and not wheat. And the commentator says that barley is the way of a storm, and red is like blood, to shed blood — these are like words of derash. And this man riding is a prince. The interpretation <i>במצולה</i> (in the depth) is difficult. And Yefet said that it is a place name and the bet is opened with pataḥ, like <i>וזבח וצלמנע בקרקר</i>. Even though it is not the way for a place name to take pataḥ, for one does not say <i>בציון</i> or <i>בשמרון</i> except with sheva or with ḥiriq. And R. Moses the Kohen said: <i>במצולה</i> is a pool of water, and myrtles are around it." "<b>and behind him horses</b> — and there is no man riding them. These are like the words of Ezekiel: <i>ופני שור מהשמאל</i> (and the face of an ox from the left). And the word <i>שרוקים</i> is from the root <i>שורקה</i> (whistling) — in the appearance of one who whistles. And these horses are many, upon three <i>עינים</i> — meaning colors."], :book :zechariah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Zecharia -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/zecharya"] ["1" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=25&perek=5&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:45:42.329511192Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}